# D-CREATE-ON-ZOMBIE-SHELL-INHERITS-DEAD-LIFE-NBLOCKS, H-Z1, the CAW leg.  The
# hypothesis, the guard and the instruments are those of
# tests/queues/zshell_nblocks_sanitize_ab.queue (2/net/mesh/mpath): a reload
# that adopts a peer's free image (P116-ZOMBIE-ADOPT) sets only the shell's
# generation and mode, the create-path recycle defers the shell as a dead shell
# and resets it only when it still has a mode, so the create inherits the dead
# life's block count.  On this configuration the H-F6 control laps pwc1 and pwc2
# (2/disk/caw/direct g2b, ~/src/mxfs-b) made 6 and 9 such creates and each
# left one core on the platter that failed xfs_dinode_verify (ino 0x800081,
# nblocks without extents), under audits that never compared block counts.
#
# Same-build A/B of module knob deadshell_sanitize_guard (0 = control, 1 =
# fix) on tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh with inact_local_epoch_guard 0 in both
# arms (that arm makes the unlinker's peer-freed verdicts end in zombie
# adopts), setattr delay 400 ms, unlink live delay 1000 ms, every other guard at
# its module default.  Runs from the main tree, rebuilt after hf6tdr's QUEUE
# DONE from the sources ~/src/mxfs-c was synced from (srcversion
# A7E5F619C93D6F05C21A1CB expected; the harness prints each lap's build and
# refuses a node running anything else), on 2/disk/caw/direct g2b.
#
# THE AUDIT is the rebuilt main tree's tools/chk_mxfs, which compares every
# live core's block count with the blocks its forks name (P-NBLOCKS-MISMATCH);
# its first run over the 25 kept images found 0 mismatches and no other change
# from the previous build.  Each lap's ZRESULT prints audit_nblocks_mismatch.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   REACHED       every control lap reads a_stale_blocks > 0.  If no control
#                 lap is reached, the window is redesigned before anything is
#                 judged.
#   PROVEN        a reached control lap reads nblocks_inherited > 0, and at
#                 least one of its P-CREATE-NBLOCKS-INHERITED lines names a
#                 number that has a P-RECYCLE-DEADSHELL-STALE line guard=0 on
#                 the same node within the preceding second (both kept in
#                 <node>_zshell.txt).  A control-lap P-NBLOCKS-MISMATCH or
#                 dinode verify failure on such a number is the defect on the
#                 platter and shows the audit sees it; it judges nothing else.
#   FIX VERIFIED  REACHED and PROVEN, and every non-vacuous fix lap
#                 (a_sanitized > 0) reads ZPASS: nblocks_inherited 0 on both
#                 nodes, dinode_verify_fail 0, audit CLEAN with
#                 audit_nblocks_mismatch 0, node_failures 0.
#   REFUTED       a non-vacuous fix lap reads nblocks_inherited > 0, a dinode
#                 verify failure, or a P-NBLOCKS-MISMATCH: trace the instance.
#   OTHER         a P-CREATE-NBLOCKS-INHERITED line on either arm whose number
#                 has no P-RECYCLE-DEADSHELL-STALE line before it (a second path
#                 into xfs_inode_init with a block count), or a control-lap
#                 P-NBLOCKS-MISMATCH on a number with no inherited create: its
#                 own finding, traced; it does not judge this guard but blocks
#                 the record's closure.
# A lap whose audit is STALE/NONE has no verdict and is rerun; a ZVACUOUS lap
# has no verdict.
#
# Bound per lap: the H-F6 CAW queue's (tests/queues/hf6_peer_last_closer_ab.queue
# in ~/src/mxfs-b, 1090 s, the sum of the harness's own step bounds) plus 2x20 s
# for the sanitize knob set/readback = 1130 s.  Its laps took 268-337 s.
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=0 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh nbcc1 0 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=1 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh nbcf1 0 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=0 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh nbcc2 0 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=1 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh nbcf2 0 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=1 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh nbcf3 0 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1130 PLC_SANITIZE_GUARD=1 tests/peer_last_closer_ab.sh nbcf4 0 40 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
